:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="dolx-changelog">
		<div class="dolx-changelog-hero">
			<span class="dolx-changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.20.15</span></h1>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="dolx-changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Added Poppy's Christmas gift event
			<ul>
				<li>You can now buy and wrap a Christmas gift for Poppy at the mall.
				</li>
				<li>You can give it to them when they are at their flat or by the lake.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added static for the pound respect.
		</li>
		<li>Added Nectar Addiction to the Statistics page, beneath Lurker Eaten.
		</li>
		<li>Updated Jordan's chastity dialogue
			<ul>
				<li>If you are an initiate, monk, nun, or priest, Jordan will now mention your temple rank when:
					<ul>
						<li>You first ask for a chastity belt, warning you that it is a serious commitment.
						</li>
						<li>You are still a virgin and ask to have the belt removed, reminding you of your vow.
						</li>
						<li>You ask about becoming a monk or nun, explaining what the temple expects from you.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Bakunawa and the Blood Moon
			<ul>
				<li>While Bakunawa is active during a blood moon, you gain the <strong>Blood Moon Resonance</strong> trait.
				</li>
				<li>This trait increases the damage you deal while fighting back by <strong>15%</strong>.
				</li>
				<li>The trait only appears during a blood moon and disappears when it ends.
				</li>
				<li>Fixed escaping the wraith nightmare before drowning leaving the world trapped under a permanent blood moon.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Added a Neutral clothing preference
			<ul>
				<li>The Identity settings now include a third Clothing Preference alongside Masculine and Feminine: <strong>Neutral: “Don’t care”</strong>.
				</li>
				<li>Clothes will not cause dysphoria or stress, but they will not provide comfort either.
				</li>
				<li>The Clothing section will be hidden from the Identity screen, similar to disabling a Body Identity category.
				</li>
				<li>You can switch back to Masculine or Feminine at any time.
				</li>
				<li>New characters using Neutral will start in overalls, since the game treats them as neither masculine nor feminine.
				</li>
				<li>Underwear, school uniforms, and swimwear have no neutral versions, so they will still follow your character's body.
				</li>
				<li>Existing saves will not change unless you select the new option.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
	</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Rebalanced Orgasm Addict stress relief
			<ul>
				<li>Previously, every orgasm removed 1,400–1,800 stress, even during rape. Several orgasms in one turn could cancel almost all stress gained during an assault, making stress pass-outs extremely unlikely in the mid or late game.
				</li>
				<li>Stress relief now depends on consent:
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Forced orgasms</strong> remove 400–600 stress, allowing repeated assault to still cause the player to pass out.
						</li>
						<li><strong>Consensual orgasms</strong> remain strongly relieving and remove about 1,000–1,286 stress.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Tweaked X-Change antidotes
			<ul>
				<li>Antidote and Antidote Forte can now be taken whenever an X-Change pill is active, even if its timer is frozen.
				</li>
				<li>If an antidote cannot shorten the pill's duration, the dose is still used but has no effect. It will not cause pain, stress, or any other changes.
				</li>
				<li>The game will tell you that the antidote did not work without revealing why. This prevents hidden conditions, such as an unnoticed pregnancy, from being spoiled.
				</li>
				<li>Antidotes are now only greyed out when you are not under the effects of an X-Change pill, and the menu will clearly explain this.
				</li>
				<li>Antidotes, anti-pills, and test strips now work correctly while Harper's cleansing treatment or the Purity trait is active.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
	</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Fixed blurry sprites and broken two-tone hair dye
			<ul>
				<li>Fixed blurry character art in the side-view, character creation, and Characteristics page.
				</li>
				<li>Fixed normal two-tone hair dye breaking after using the special vanilla two-tone hairstyle.
				</li>
				<li>Fixed hair colours and the side-view sometimes changing after refreshing the page.
				</li>
				<li>Affected saves will be repaired automatically when loaded.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed Avery bedroom event overlap
			<ul>
				<li>Avery's return-from-work scene could appear at the same time as the unread letter event in their bedroom, causing both scenes to overlap.
				</li>
				<li>The letter will now wait until your next visit.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed Bailey scenes losing Bailey mid-scene
			<ul>
				<li>The game can also automatically repair damaged named NPC data in older saves. This prevents characters from using another NPC's pronouns, title, or body description.
				</li>
				<li>Invalid pronouns will also be repaired. For example, Bailey should no longer be called <strong>“it”</strong>.
				</li>
				<li>These repairs do not change the NPC's body, genitals, breasts, or relationship values. The Ivory Wraith will continue using <strong>“it”</strong> as intended.
				</li>
				<li>A one-time message will appear when either repair is made.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed hypnosis traits and trance effects
			<ul>
				<li>Hypnotic Deviancy, Hypnotic Yearning, Hypnotic Flaunting, and Hypnotic Crossdressing can now be gained correctly after the first hypnosis session.
				</li>
				<li>Previously, the game said the trait had “deepened” before it had actually been gained, so two sessions were required.
				</li>
				<li>Hypnotic Deviancy will no longer use up its activation chance when the beast is not approaching you.
				</li>
				<li>The town stray dog and island snake will no longer repeat <strong>“You break free from your trance.”</strong> every round.
				</li>
				<li>Trance effects now last for the intended two rounds and end with a single message.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Fixed bathroom “Scoop Out” scenes
			<ul>
				<li>The scene now correctly names the clothes you are wearing instead of saying <strong>“your naked.”</strong>
				</li>
				<li>The <strong>Scoop out vagina</strong> option no longer appears if you do not have a vagina.
				</li>
				<li>Fluids left behind after changing body parts will no longer create a broken option that wastes five minutes and cannot be cleared.
				</li>
				<li>Park and school toilets now temporarily remove worn dildos and butt plugs, then put them back afterwards, matching the home bathroom.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
	</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon images" aria-hidden="true">&#128444;</span> Art and Image Updates</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Updated Melusine sprites
			<ul>
				<li>Melusine no longer copies the player character's hair colour and now uses their own individual colours.
				</li>
				<li>Added a purple variant by Axos.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Updated Water Dragon skin colours
			<ul>
				<li>Soft Pink is now more pastel.
				</li>
				<li>Added a Sky Blue colour.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
	</ul>
	</div>
<</widget>>
